{
  "heading": "Shape the answers Tachyon makes itself, in every Yon language",
  "axis": "language",
  "summary": "Tachyon answers some requests itself: 401 without an identity, 403 without a role, 500 when the identity provider fails, 400 for a bad value or body, 413 for a body over the limit, 422 for broken @Checked rules, and 500 when the route could not answer. Name one of the seven built-in error types on a @HandlesError method, and that method writes the body. Tachyon keeps the status, so the method takes no ResponseStatus (ADR 0136).",
  "body": "Choose a language below. `OrdersController` says `Allow(Admin)`. `AppIdentityProvider` knows two sessions, `ada-token` (with the role `Admin`) and `bob-token` (no roles), and fails for `broken-token`. `OrdersErrorHandler` has one method for each built-in type, and each method answers a `Problem` with a code and a numbered message, such as `{\"code\":\"not_signed_in\",\"message\":\"[MS0001]: Sign in again.\"}`.\n\n- `GET /orders` without a token answers 401 from `NotSignedIn`; with `bob-token`, 403 from `RoleMissing`; with `broken-token`, 500 from `IdentityCheckFailed`.\n- `POST /orders` with `ada-token` and the body `{` answers 400 from `RequestRejected` (`part` is `body`). A body over `yon.server.maxbody` answers 413 from `BodyTooLarge`. `{\"name\":\"\",\"level\":0}` answers 422 from `CheckRejected`, whose `violations` list `level:Min`, `name:NotEmpty` and `name:Length`.\n- `GET /orders` with `ada-token` fails with an error that no method takes, so `UnexpectedError` answers 500.\n\nEvery shaped answer keeps Tachyon's status and has the `x-tachyon-request-id` header; the error's `reference` field holds the same id. The handler never sees the `authorization` or `cookie` header, the identity provider's error or the request body. If a method is missing, the answer stays as Tachyon writes it. If the method fails, Tachyon sends its own answer and logs `error_handler.failed`.",
